nt-time"><a href=3D"https://css-tricks.com/illustrator-to-svg/#comment-1605=
082"><span class=3D"screen-reader">Permalink to comment</span>#</a> <time d=
atetime=3D"2016-11-20T07:16:49-07:00">November 20, 2016</time></div>
      </div>

     =20
      <div class=3D"comment-content">

        <p>Just a quick side note, if you are planning on using <strong>SVG=
 external sprites</strong>, <a href=3D"https://css-tricks.com/svg-use-with-=
external-reference-take-2/" rel=3D"ugc">see css-tricks article</a>  prefer =
exporting presentation attributes to styles as they will render better. The=
 use of classes in those files will make them conflict with each other if t=
hey are in the same file.</p>
<p>On the same note, for SVG sprites, avoid using gradients as they will ap=
